# SYNOPSIS

```ndb
service=simplefb program=/boot/bin/drv-simplefb
    post=simplefb console framebuffer when=vx.display
```

# DESCRIPTION

`drv-simplefb` serves the framebuffer the firmware left (x86's GOP, aarch64's ramfb) as a back end of the display engine protocol (docs/proto/display.md, ADR-0026), to displayd(8).
svcd(8) hands it the framebuffer as a physical VMO with its `framebuffer` flag; it maps it write-combining (ADR-0051).

It has one output in the firmware's mode and one layer, an image or a colour the screen's size or smaller, unscaled and upright.
An applied image is copied into the framebuffer at the next vblank, its damage only, converted if the framebuffer's channels are not XRGB8888's.
A framebuffer has no vblank interrupt: its vblank is a timer at 60 Hz, since a GOP gives no refresh.

It serves one session at a time on `/srv/simplefb`, and refuses a second with `BAD_STATE`.
It saves the screen when a session opens and puts it back when the session ends, so the boot console shows again if displayd exits (ADR-0026 item 3).

# SEE ALSO

displayd(8), svc(6), vmo(2)

# BUGS

The 60 Hz is assumed, not read.
Only 32-bit framebuffers.
